Strictly speaking, there is rest but there is not safe rest.

"." dot rests in the current spot on the currnet level.  Which
means monsters on the level or spwaned there come after
you.

" " space can be set to do the same.  See the "restonspace"
flag in the config file as described in the guidebook.txt file.
but it is no more safe than dot.

"s" searches for traps, secret doors and so on.  It makes
sense at times to move along a wall searching.  You heal
gradually, get hungrier gradually, and maybe find hidden
rooms.  All on the current level with newly spawned monsters
going after you.

A simple strategy is to notice that monster strength is
determined by averaging your XP level and your depth.  Move
up a level and the monsters are slightly weaker on average.
This is typically enough that you are no longer in mortal
danger.  There's also the aspect that the level above was
already cleared out so you only have to deal with newly
spawned monsters.

But the biggest answer is the strategic one - "An ounce of
prevention is worth a pound of cure".  If you start losing hit
points retreat before you are in trouble so you don't need to
heal.


